## Why this version is safe to use

These issues from the earlier draft have already been handled:

- the project now pins **AGP `8.6.1`**, which supports `compileSdk = 35`
- the Gradle wrapper is pinned to **Gradle `8.7`**
- `gradle.properties` is included
- `proguard-rules.pro` is included
- launcher icon resources are included
- the base site URL is configured in one place in `app/build.gradle.kts`
- the manifest host is derived from that URL through a manifest placeholder
- the Kotlin compile errors found during a real build were fixed

## Replace before shipping

Edit only this line in:

```text
GoldenAutomotiveWebApp/app/build.gradle.kts
```

Replace:

```kotlin
val appBaseUrl = "https://your-live-site.com"
```

With your real production origin, for example:

```kotlin
val appBaseUrl = "https://app.example.com"
```

Use the root origin only:
- good: `https://app.example.com`
- avoid: `https://app.example.com/some/path`

The deep link host is derived automatically from that URL, so you do not need to edit the manifest separately anymore.

